ted': "ValidationResult.isSuccess() == true and the dynamic anchor '#myAnchor' is registered in the ExecutionContext", 'description': 'The schema is marked as a dynamic anchor (isDynamicAnchor() returns true). When validateAndCollect is invoked the method should store the anchor URI in the ExecutionContext without producing validation errors.'}]}, {'group': 'Keyword walk listener execution', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "name": "Alice" }'}], 'expected': "ValidationResult.isSuccess() == true and the configured WalkListenerRunner's onWalkStart/onWalkEnd callbacks are invoked exactly once", 'description': 'The JsonSchema instance has a non‑null keywordWalkListenerRunner. During validateAndCollect the method must delegate to the runner before and after walking the schema, ensuring the listener callbacks are executed.'}]}, {'group': 'Switch‑case branch for $ref handling', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Address" }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == true and the referenced schema is resolved and validated', 'description': 'When the schema contains a $ref keyword the method enters the switch‑case that resolves the reference via getRefSchemaNode(). The test verifies that the referenced schema is correctly retrieved, validated and that no extra errors are produced.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "$ref": "#/nonexistent" }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == false and contains a message indicating unresolved reference', 'description': 'If the $ref cannot be resolved, the switch‑case should add an appropriate error message and return a failing ValidationResult.'}]}, {'group': 'If‑else branch for atRoot() flag', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "root": true }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == true and the method treats the node as the root (atRoot() == true)', 'description': 'When the call originates from the public validateAndCollect(JsonNode) overload, atRoot() returns true. The method must follow the branch that sets the initial path to "$" and validates accordingly.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "nested": { "value": 1 } }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == true and the method processes the node as a non‑root child schema (atRoot() == false)', 'description': 'When validateAndCollect is invoked internally (e.g., from a child schema), atRoot() returns false, causing the method to take the else branch that prefixes the path with the parent location.'}]}, {'group': 'Enum validator success', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "color": "red" }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == true and ValidationResult.getMessages() is empty', 'description': 'The schema defines an enum [\'red\',\'green\',\'blue\'] for property "color". The supplied node contains a value that is part of the enum, so the enum validator does not add any messages.'}]}, {'group': 'Enum validator failure', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "color": "yellow" }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == false and contains a message with type = "enum" indicating the value is not allowed', 'description': 'The schema defines an enum [\'red\',\'green\',\'blue\'] for property "color". The supplied value "yellow" is not in the list, triggering the enum validator.'}]}, {'group': 'Const validator failure', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "status": "pending" }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == false and contains a message with type = "const" indicating the constant value mismatch', 'description': 'The schema contains a const keyword with value "active" for property "status". The node provides a different value, causing the const validator to fail.'}]}, {'group': 'Pattern validator failure', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "email": "not-an-email" }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == false and contains a message with type = "pattern" indicating regex mismatch', 'description': 'The schema defines a pattern "^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$" for property "email". The supplied string does not match, so the pattern validator adds an error.'}]}, {'group': 'Minimum number validator failure', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "age": 15 }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == false and contains a message with type = "minimum" indicating the value is less than the allowed minimum', 'description': 'The schema sets a minimum of 18 for property "age". The node provides 15, which violates the minimum constraint.'}]}, {'group': 'Array items type mismatch', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "tags": [ "valid", 123, "alsoValid" ] }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == false and contains a message with type = "type" for the second array element indicating expected type "string" but found "integer"', 'description': 'The schema defines "items" with a type "string" for array property "tags". The second element is an integer, causing the items validator to report a type error.'}]}, {'group': 'OneOf validator success (one subschema matches)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "value": 42 }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == true and ValidationResult.getMessages() is empty', 'description': 'The schema uses a oneOf with two alternatives: one expects an integer, the other expects a string. The node provides an integer, satisfying the first alternative, so validation succeeds.'}]}, {'group': 'OneOf validator failure (none match)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{ "value": true }'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult.isSuccess() == false and contains a message with type = "oneOf" indicating that none of the subschemas matched', 'description': "The schema's oneOf alternatives accept only numbers or strings. The node supplies a